~ stone_1

Unknown: Somebody went to the trouble of a headstone. The least I can do is read it. [ID:HINT_STONE_1]

=> END

~ stone_2

Unknown: That gravestone. There's lettering on it, what's left of it. [ID:HINT_STONE_2]

=> END

~ stone_3

Unknown: The gravestone, up close. The name, and the words under it. [ID:HINT_STONE_3]

=> END

~ gravedigger_1

Unknown: Somebody dug the grave I climbed out of. Graves don't dig themselves. [ID:HINT_GRAVEDIGGER_1]

=> END

~ gravedigger_2

Unknown: There was a gate west of my grave. Somebody's working there. [ID:HINT_GRAVEDIGGER_2]

=> END

~ gravedigger_3

Unknown: West of the grave, at the gate. Talk to the Gravedigger. [ID:HINT_GRAVEDIGGER_3]

=> END

~ register_1

Unknown: A gravedigger keeps records. Someone has to. [ID:HINT_REGISTER_1]

=> END

~ register_2

Unknown: His lodge, by the gate. There was a book on a lectern. [ID:HINT_REGISTER_2]

=> END

~ register_3

Unknown: In the Gravedigger's lodge, read the book on the lectern. [ID:HINT_REGISTER_3]

=> END

~ ossuary_key_1

Unknown: The book said which key. I only have to believe it. [ID:HINT_OSSUARY_KEY_1]

=> END

~ ossuary_key_2

Unknown: Key thirteen, on the wall in the lodge. [ID:HINT_OSSUARY_KEY_2]

=> END

~ ossuary_key_3

Unknown: Take key thirteen from the key wall in the lodge. [ID:HINT_OSSUARY_KEY_3]

=> END

~ crypt_1

Unknown: A key is only interesting next to a lock. [ID:HINT_CRYPT_1]

=> END

~ crypt_2

Unknown: The crypt steps at the gate, under the chapel. [ID:HINT_CRYPT_2]

=> END

~ crypt_3

Unknown: Use the ossuary key on the crypt steps by the gate. [ID:HINT_CRYPT_3]

=> END

~ glass_1

Unknown: The crow brought its treasures somewhere down here. [ID:HINT_GLASS_1]

=> END

~ glass_2

Unknown: High up in the ossuary, on the ledge. A nest. [ID:HINT_GLASS_2]

=> END

~ glass_3

Unknown: Take the glass from the crow's nest in the ossuary. [ID:HINT_GLASS_3]

=> END

~ mend_1

Unknown: A lantern glass is wasted in my hands. [ID:HINT_MEND_1]

=> END

~ mend_2

Unknown: The Gravedigger lost exactly this. [ID:HINT_MEND_2]

=> END

~ mend_3

Unknown: Give the lantern glass to the Gravedigger. [ID:HINT_MEND_3]

=> END

~ sister_1

Unknown: The cathedral had more doors than the one I came in by. [ID:HINT_SISTER_1]

=> END

~ sister_2

Unknown: An arch in the nave's aisle, with moonlight beyond. Someone's out there. [ID:HINT_SISTER_2]

=> END

~ sister_3

Unknown: Through the arch in the nave, to the cloister. Talk to the Sister. [ID:HINT_SISTER_3]

=> END

~ dove_1

Unknown: The stone was signed by a dove. The Sister has been here a long time. [ID:HINT_DOVE_1]

=> END

~ dove_2

Unknown: Ask the Sister whether she knew anyone called the dove. [ID:HINT_DOVE_2]

=> END

~ dove_3

Unknown: Ask the Sister about the dove. [ID:HINT_DOVE_3]

=> END

~ book_request_1

Unknown: Those doors in the nave lead to the city. Somebody holds the key. [ID:HINT_BOOK_REQUEST_1]

=> END

~ book_request_2

Unknown: The Sister has the key. Tell her I need to get into the city. [ID:HINT_BOOK_REQUEST_2]

=> END

~ book_request_3

Unknown: Ask the Sister about getting into the city. [ID:HINT_BOOK_REQUEST_3]

=> END

~ singer_1

Unknown: The dove's hymn book is up in the choir loft. In the dark. [ID:HINT_SINGER_1]

=> END

~ singer_2

Unknown: The turret stair in the cloister. I'll need the Gravedigger's lantern to see. [ID:HINT_SINGER_2]

=> END

~ singer_3

Unknown: With the lantern, climb the turret to the choir loft and touch the hymn book. [ID:HINT_SINGER_3]

=> END

~ book_1

Unknown: That book has done remembering for me. Now it should go to someone who'll keep it. [ID:HINT_BOOK_1]

=> END

~ book_2

Unknown: The hymn book, on its stand in the loft. [ID:HINT_BOOK_2]

=> END

~ book_3

Unknown: Take the hymn book from its stand. [ID:HINT_BOOK_3]

=> END

~ west_key_1

Unknown: The Sister wanted something of hers. I have it. [ID:HINT_WEST_KEY_1]

=> END

~ west_key_2

Unknown: Give the Sister the hymn book. [ID:HINT_WEST_KEY_2]

=> END

~ west_key_3

Unknown: Give the hymn book to the Sister in the cloister. [ID:HINT_WEST_KEY_3]

=> END

~ doors_1

Unknown: A key, and a city on the other side of a door. [ID:HINT_DOORS_1]

=> END

~ doors_2

Unknown: The great doors, on the right of the nave. [ID:HINT_DOORS_2]

=> END

~ doors_3

Unknown: Use the west door key on the great doors in the nave. [ID:HINT_DOORS_3]

=> END

~ ch1_square_1

Unknown: The doors are open. Whoever I was, he walked these streets. [ID:HINT_CH1_SQUARE_1]

=> END

~ ch1_square_2

Unknown: Through the great doors in the nave, into the city. [ID:HINT_CH1_SQUARE_2]

=> END

~ ch1_square_3

Unknown: Use the great doors in the nave. [ID:HINT_CH1_SQUARE_3]

=> END

~ crier_1

Unknown: Somebody's shouting in the square. News might help. [ID:HINT_CRIER_1]

=> END

~ crier_2

Unknown: The Crier, on his platform in the cathedral square. [ID:HINT_CRIER_2]

=> END

~ crier_3

Unknown: Talk to the Crier in the square. [ID:HINT_CRIER_3]

=> END

~ lamplighter_1

Unknown: The lamp street. Someone's lighting lamps that don't light. [ID:HINT_LAMPLIGHTER_1]

=> END

~ lamplighter_2

Unknown: Left of the square, the street of lamps. Talk to the Lamplighter. [ID:HINT_LAMPLIGHTER_2]

=> END

~ lamplighter_3

Unknown: Talk to the Lamplighter on the street of lamps. [ID:HINT_LAMPLIGHTER_3]

=> END

~ clockmaker_1

Unknown: A stopped clock, and somebody keeping it ready. [ID:HINT_CLOCKMAKER_1]

=> END

~ clockmaker_2

Unknown: Past the market and over the bridge, at the foot of the tower. [ID:HINT_CLOCKMAKER_2]

=> END

~ clockmaker_3

Unknown: Talk to the Clockmaker under the clock tower. [ID:HINT_CLOCKMAKER_3]

=> END

~ wedding_1

Unknown: The saint in the market wears a ribbon somebody tied for a reason. [ID:HINT_WEDDING_1]

=> END

~ wedding_2

Unknown: Touch the ribbon on the weeping saint in the market. [ID:HINT_WEDDING_2]

=> END

~ wedding_3

Unknown: Use the ribbon on the saint's wrist, in the market square. [ID:HINT_WEDDING_3]

=> END

~ candle_1

Unknown: The wedding went up the alley, to the tavern. Something of it might still be there. [ID:HINT_CANDLE_1]

=> END

~ candle_2

Unknown: The tavern, up the alley. The mantel. [ID:HINT_CANDLE_2]

=> END

~ candle_3

Unknown: Take the candle stub from the tavern mantel. [ID:HINT_CANDLE_3]

=> END

~ mathis_1

Unknown: A wedding candle, and a man who wants one warm flame. [ID:HINT_MATHIS_1]

=> END

~ mathis_2

Unknown: Give the wedding candle to the Lamplighter. [ID:HINT_MATHIS_2]

=> END

~ mathis_3

Unknown: Give the candle to the Lamplighter on the street of lamps. [ID:HINT_MATHIS_3]

=> END

~ winding_key_1

Unknown: The Clockmaker pawned his key. The Broker deals in stories, not money. [ID:HINT_WINDING_KEY_1]

=> END

~ winding_key_2

Unknown: The Broker wants something with a story in it. I have a lantern someone mended for a stranger. [ID:HINT_WINDING_KEY_2]

=> END

~ winding_key_3

Unknown: Give the Gravedigger's lantern to the Broker in his shop. [ID:HINT_WINDING_KEY_3]

=> END

~ eleven_1

Unknown: The clock has to be set to the hour it stopped. Somebody announced that hour once. [ID:HINT_ELEVEN_1]

=> END

~ eleven_2

Unknown: The Crier's last headline. Or the edicts in the alley. [ID:HINT_ELEVEN_2]

=> END

~ eleven_3

Unknown: Ask the Crier for the latest news. [ID:HINT_ELEVEN_3]

=> END

~ apprentice_1

Unknown: The clock remembers better than the Clockmaker, he said. [ID:HINT_APPRENTICE_1]

=> END

~ apprentice_2

Unknown: Inside the clock, with the warm lamp. Touch the escapement. [ID:HINT_APPRENTICE_2]

=> END

~ apprentice_3

Unknown: With the warm lamp, go into the clock and use the escapement. [ID:HINT_APPRENTICE_3]

=> END

~ escapement_1

Unknown: I know where the pin goes now. [ID:HINT_ESCAPEMENT_1]

=> END

~ escapement_2

Unknown: The escapement, inside the clock. Third tooth. [ID:HINT_ESCAPEMENT_2]

=> END

~ escapement_3

Unknown: Use the escapement again: the pin on the third tooth. [ID:HINT_ESCAPEMENT_3]

=> END

~ wound_1

Unknown: The clock needs its key turned. [ID:HINT_WOUND_1]

=> END

~ wound_2

Unknown: The winding post, beside the escapement. [ID:HINT_WOUND_2]

=> END

~ wound_3

Unknown: Use the winding key on the winding post. [ID:HINT_WOUND_3]

=> END

~ strike_1

Unknown: Behind the face, the hands. Eleven bells. [ID:HINT_STRIKE_1]

=> END

~ strike_2

Unknown: Climb the ladder to the clock face and set the hands. [ID:HINT_STRIKE_2]

=> END

~ strike_3

Unknown: Behind the clock face, use the hands. [ID:HINT_STRIKE_3]

=> END

~ lower_gate_1

Unknown: The clock struck, and something below opened. [ID:HINT_LOWER_GATE_1]

=> END

~ lower_gate_2

Unknown: Down the stair from the tower square, to the lower gate. [ID:HINT_LOWER_GATE_2]

=> END

~ lower_gate_3

Unknown: Go through the open portcullis at the lower gate. [ID:HINT_LOWER_GATE_3]

=> END

~ ch2_quarter_arrive_1

Unknown: The lower gate is open. Down, then. [ID:HINT_CH2_QUARTER_ARRIVE_1]

=> END

~ ch2_quarter_arrive_2

Unknown: Down the stair from the tower square, through the lower gate. [ID:HINT_CH2_QUARTER_ARRIVE_2]

=> END

~ ch2_quarter_arrive_3

Unknown: Go through the portcullis at the lower gate. [ID:HINT_CH2_QUARTER_ARRIVE_3]

=> END

~ ferry_bell_1

Unknown: Nobody walks in this quarter. Somebody must row. [ID:HINT_FERRY_BELL_1]

=> END

~ ferry_bell_2

Unknown: The bell on the post at the foot of the stair. [ID:HINT_FERRY_BELL_2]

=> END

~ ferry_bell_3

Unknown: Ring the ferry bell on the flooded stair. [ID:HINT_FERRY_BELL_3]

=> END

~ fare_1

Unknown: The Ferryman wants a fare I can afford. [ID:HINT_FARE_1]

=> END

~ fare_2

Unknown: A small memory, he said. Something warm I won't miss. [ID:HINT_FARE_2]

=> END

~ fare_3

Unknown: Talk to the Ferryman and give him the taste of bread. [ID:HINT_FARE_3]

=> END

~ crate_1

Unknown: Something floating in the drowned street could be useful. [ID:HINT_CRATE_1]

=> END

~ crate_2

Unknown: The crate bobbing against the wall in the drowned street. [ID:HINT_CRATE_2]

=> END

~ crate_3

Unknown: Take the crate in the drowned street. [ID:HINT_CRATE_3]

=> END

~ window_1

Unknown: The sluice house window is just out of reach. [ID:HINT_WINDOW_1]

=> END

~ window_2

Unknown: Something to stand on, under the window. [ID:HINT_WINDOW_2]

=> END

~ window_3

Unknown: Use the crate on the sluice house window. [ID:HINT_WINDOW_3]

=> END

~ petition_1

Unknown: The sluice house remembers how it worked. [ID:HINT_PETITION_1]

=> END

~ petition_2

Unknown: Touch the great gate wheel in the sluice house. [ID:HINT_PETITION_2]

=> END

~ petition_3

Unknown: Use the gate wheel in the sluice house. [ID:HINT_PETITION_3]

=> END

~ maud_1

Unknown: The Washerwoman doesn't know whose A it is. I do. [ID:HINT_MAUD_1]

=> END

~ maud_2

Unknown: Tell the Washerwoman about Aldous. [ID:HINT_MAUD_2]

=> END

~ maud_3

Unknown: At the washing steps, tell her the A is for Aldous. [ID:HINT_MAUD_3]

=> END

~ oath_1

Unknown: The doctor promised something, once. Somewhere holy. [ID:HINT_OATH_1]

=> END

~ oath_2

Unknown: The drowned chapel, over the rooftops from the drowned street. The altar. [ID:HINT_OATH_2]

=> END

~ oath_3

Unknown: Use the altar in the drowned chapel. [ID:HINT_OATH_3]

=> END

~ doctor_1

Unknown: The doctor forgot her own oath. I heard it. [ID:HINT_DOCTOR_1]

=> END

~ doctor_2

Unknown: Say her oath back to the Plague Doctor. [ID:HINT_DOCTOR_2]

=> END

~ doctor_3

Unknown: In the hospice, give the Plague Doctor her oath. [ID:HINT_DOCTOR_3]

=> END

~ dedication_1

Unknown: The aqueduct was opened with a ceremony. The plaque would remember. [ID:HINT_DEDICATION_1]

=> END

~ dedication_2

Unknown: Past the washing steps, through the drowned forest, to the aqueduct's foot. The plaque. [ID:HINT_DEDICATION_2]

=> END

~ dedication_3

Unknown: Use the plaque at the aqueduct's foot. [ID:HINT_DEDICATION_3]

=> END

~ seal_1

Unknown: That seal on the plaque. I've seen it before. On my own hand. [ID:HINT_SEAL_1]

=> END

~ seal_2

Unknown: The seal ring, on the plaque. [ID:HINT_SEAL_2]

=> END

~ seal_3

Unknown: Use the seal ring on the plaque at the aqueduct's foot. [ID:HINT_SEAL_3]

=> END

~ span_1

Unknown: The aqueduct is broken. Something long would cross it. [ID:HINT_SPAN_1]

=> END

~ span_2

Unknown: The doctor's stretcher, across the gap. [ID:HINT_SPAN_2]

=> END

~ span_3

Unknown: On the aqueduct, use the stretcher on the gap. [ID:HINT_SPAN_3]

=> END

~ valve_door_1

Unknown: The valve house is sealed with a seal I know. [ID:HINT_VALVE_DOOR_1]

=> END

~ valve_door_2

Unknown: The seal ring on the valve house door. [ID:HINT_VALVE_DOOR_2]

=> END

~ valve_door_3

Unknown: Use the seal ring on the valve house door. [ID:HINT_VALVE_DOOR_3]

=> END

~ valve_1

Unknown: The valve is chained and padlocked. [ID:HINT_VALVE_1]

=> END

~ valve_2

Unknown: Aldous's key, from the Washerwoman. [ID:HINT_VALVE_2]

=> END

~ valve_3

Unknown: Use the sluice key on the valve. [ID:HINT_VALVE_3]

=> END

~ signing_1

Unknown: Turn it. Whatever it shows me. [ID:HINT_SIGNING_1]

=> END

~ signing_2

Unknown: Use the valve. [ID:HINT_SIGNING_2]

=> END

~ signing_3

Unknown: Use the valve in the valve house. [ID:HINT_SIGNING_3]

=> END

~ ch3_avenue_1

Unknown: Corin was going upstream, to the city on the hill. [ID:HINT_CH3_AVENUE_1]

=> END

~ ch3_avenue_2

Unknown: The valve house: Corin's ferry goes on to the upper city. [ID:HINT_CH3_AVENUE_2]

=> END

~ ch3_avenue_3

Unknown: Turn the valve, and ride with Corin. [ID:HINT_CH3_AVENUE_3]

=> END

~ hangman_1

Unknown: A gallows, off the avenue. Somebody tends it. [ID:HINT_HANGMAN_1]

=> END

~ hangman_2

Unknown: Through the archway on the left of the avenue, to the gallows square. [ID:HINT_HANGMAN_2]

=> END

~ hangman_3

Unknown: Talk to the Hangman in the gallows square. [ID:HINT_HANGMAN_3]

=> END

~ refusal_1

Unknown: The gallows beam is worn by one pair of hands. [ID:HINT_REFUSAL_1]

=> END

~ refusal_2

Unknown: Touch the gallows beam. [ID:HINT_REFUSAL_2]

=> END

~ refusal_3

Unknown: Use the gallows beam in the gallows square. [ID:HINT_REFUSAL_3]

=> END

~ chain_key_1

Unknown: The Hangman refused once. He should know. [ID:HINT_CHAIN_KEY_1]

=> END

~ chain_key_2

Unknown: Tell the Hangman he refused, once. [ID:HINT_CHAIN_KEY_2]

=> END

~ chain_key_3

Unknown: Talk to the Hangman: 'You refused, once. I saw it.' [ID:HINT_CHAIN_KEY_3]

=> END

~ theater_1

Unknown: A theatre, chained shut. A key would help. [ID:HINT_THEATER_1]

=> END

~ theater_2

Unknown: The Hangman's key, on the theatre doors. [ID:HINT_THEATER_2]

=> END

~ theater_3

Unknown: Use the chain key on the theatre's doors. [ID:HINT_THEATER_3]

=> END

~ show_1

Unknown: A puppeteer with no audience. [ID:HINT_SHOW_1]

=> END

~ show_2

Unknown: Talk to the Puppeteer on the stage, and watch her play. [ID:HINT_SHOW_2]

=> END

~ show_3

Unknown: Ask the Puppeteer to show you the play. [ID:HINT_SHOW_3]

=> END

~ quill_1

Unknown: The clerk puppet backstage holds a real clerk's quill. [ID:HINT_QUILL_1]

=> END

~ quill_2

Unknown: Through the wings, backstage. The clerk puppet. [ID:HINT_QUILL_2]

=> END

~ quill_3

Unknown: Use the clerk puppet backstage to take the quill. [ID:HINT_QUILL_3]

=> END

~ records_gate_1

Unknown: The Hall of Records is sealed with my seal. [ID:HINT_RECORDS_GATE_1]

=> END

~ records_gate_2

Unknown: The ring, on the records gate's lock. [ID:HINT_RECORDS_GATE_2]

=> END

~ records_gate_3

Unknown: Use the seal ring on the gate of the Hall of Records. [ID:HINT_RECORDS_GATE_3]

=> END

~ sign_in_1

Unknown: 'All who enter shall sign.' I have a quill now. [ID:HINT_SIGN_IN_1]

=> END

~ sign_in_2

Unknown: The visitors' register on the lectern in the hall. [ID:HINT_SIGN_IN_2]

=> END

~ sign_in_3

Unknown: Use the clerk's quill on the visitors' register. [ID:HINT_SIGN_IN_3]

=> END

~ office_ref_1

Unknown: The stacks keep an index of every name. The Dove's will be there. [ID:HINT_OFFICE_REF_1]

=> END

~ office_ref_2

Unknown: Through the archway on the left of the hall, to the stacks. The index. [ID:HINT_OFFICE_REF_2]

=> END

~ office_ref_3

Unknown: In the stacks, look at the index, and find the Dove's entry. [ID:HINT_OFFICE_REF_3]

=> END

~ permit_1

Unknown: My office is locked, and the Registrar has the keys. [ID:HINT_PERMIT_1]

=> END

~ permit_2

Unknown: Ask the Registrar to let me into my office. [ID:HINT_PERMIT_2]

=> END

~ permit_3

Unknown: Talk to the Registrar: 'I want to see my office.' [ID:HINT_PERMIT_3]

=> END

~ office_1

Unknown: My desk remembers what I did there. [ID:HINT_OFFICE_1]

=> END

~ office_2

Unknown: Sit at my desk. Touch it. [ID:HINT_OFFICE_2]

=> END

~ office_3

Unknown: Use the desk in the Magistrate's office, and in the past, the Ledger on it. [ID:HINT_OFFICE_3]

=> END

~ vault_1

Unknown: The vault opens to one word I wrote once. [ID:HINT_VAULT_1]

=> END

~ vault_2

Unknown: The word I wrote on the Ledger's first leaf: SILENCE. [ID:HINT_VAULT_2]

=> END

~ vault_3

Unknown: Use the vault door in the Registrar's chamber and choose SILENCE. [ID:HINT_VAULT_3]

=> END

~ bridge_1

Unknown: He's taken the book up toward the cathedral. [ID:HINT_BRIDGE_1]

=> END

~ bridge_2

Unknown: Through the vault, the passage, the covered bridge. [ID:HINT_BRIDGE_2]

=> END

~ bridge_3

Unknown: Go through the vault to the covered bridge, and out the far door. [ID:HINT_BRIDGE_3]

=> END

~ ch4_roof_1

Unknown: The Registrar ran for the cathedral's heights. [ID:HINT_CH4_ROOF_1]

=> END

~ ch4_roof_2

Unknown: Across the covered bridge, through the far door. [ID:HINT_CH4_ROOF_2]

=> END

~ ch4_roof_3

Unknown: Use the far door at the end of the covered bridge. [ID:HINT_CH4_ROOF_3]

=> END

~ stone_1

Unknown: A gap ahead will need filling. [ID:HINT_STONE_1]

=> END

~ stone_2

Unknown: The loose stone block on the roof ridge. [ID:HINT_STONE_2]

=> END

~ stone_3

Unknown: Take the loose stone on the cathedral roof. [ID:HINT_STONE_3]

=> END

~ buttress_1

Unknown: The buttress walk has a slab missing. [ID:HINT_BUTTRESS_1]

=> END

~ buttress_2

Unknown: Put the loose stone in the gap. [ID:HINT_BUTTRESS_2]

=> END

~ buttress_3

Unknown: Use the loose stone on the gap in the buttress walk. [ID:HINT_BUTTRESS_3]

=> END

~ dovecote_key_1

Unknown: The dovecote is locked. A bird would hide a key somewhere high. [ID:HINT_DOVECOTE_KEY_1]

=> END

~ dovecote_key_2

Unknown: One of the gargoyles has something in its mouth. [ID:HINT_DOVECOTE_KEY_2]

=> END

~ dovecote_key_3

Unknown: Take the key from the gargoyle's jaws. [ID:HINT_DOVECOTE_KEY_3]

=> END

~ dove_1

Unknown: Someone lives in the dovecote. [ID:HINT_DOVE_1]

=> END

~ dove_2

Unknown: The dovecote key, on the dovecote door. [ID:HINT_DOVE_2]

=> END

~ dove_3

Unknown: Use the dovecote key on the dovecote's door, and talk to her. [ID:HINT_DOVE_3]

=> END

~ letter_1

Unknown: She said there's a letter on her desk. [ID:HINT_LETTER_1]

=> END

~ letter_2

Unknown: Down the trapdoor to her room. The desk. [ID:HINT_LETTER_2]

=> END

~ letter_3

Unknown: In the Dove's room, take the letter from the desk. [ID:HINT_LETTER_3]

=> END

~ forgive_1

Unknown: That letter was always meant for her. [ID:HINT_FORGIVE_1]

=> END

~ forgive_2

Unknown: Give the Dove the letter. [ID:HINT_FORGIVE_2]

=> END

~ forgive_3

Unknown: Give the unsent letter to the Dove. [ID:HINT_FORGIVE_3]

=> END

~ song_1

Unknown: The rose window watched the night I took her name. [ID:HINT_SONG_1]

=> END

~ song_2

Unknown: Through the tower door, to the ledge behind the rose window. Touch the window. [ID:HINT_SONG_2]

=> END

~ song_3

Unknown: Use the rose window. [ID:HINT_SONG_3]

=> END

~ edmund_1

Unknown: He was my first entry. I know his name. [ID:HINT_EDMUND_1]

=> END

~ edmund_2

Unknown: Say his name to him: Edmund Vey. [ID:HINT_EDMUND_2]

=> END

~ edmund_3

Unknown: Talk to the Registrar in the bell chamber and give him his name. [ID:HINT_EDMUND_3]

=> END

~ ring_1

Unknown: The bell carries to everyone who ever had a name. [ID:HINT_RING_1]

=> END

~ ring_2

Unknown: Up the ladder to the belfry, with the book. [ID:HINT_RING_2]

=> END

~ ring_3

Unknown: Use the Ledger on the great bell. [ID:HINT_RING_3]

=> END

~ none

Unknown: Nothing pulls at me right now. The rest of me is still out there, somewhere. [ID:HINT_NONE_1]

=> END
